examples.question_text:
By finding the product of their gradients, show that the blue line $\ell_1$ and the red dashed line $\ell_2$ are perpendicular.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{lineblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{linered}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=7mm,color=gridgrey,thin] (-4,-4) grid (4,4);
\draw[black,-{Stealth}] (-4.3,0) -- (4.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,-{Stealth}] (0,-4.3) -- (0,4.4) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \v in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} {
\draw[black] (\v,0.07) -- (\v,-0.07);
\path (\v,-0.12) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};
\draw[black] (0.07,\v) -- (-0.07,\v);
\path (-0.12,\v) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};
}
\path (-0.12,-0.12) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\draw[lineblue,thick] (-4,-1) -- (4,3);
\draw[linered,thick,dashed] (-2.5,4) -- (1.5,-4);
\path (3.3,2.9) node[above,text=lineblue] {$\ell_1$};
\path (1.25,-3.5) node[right,text=linered] {$\ell_2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
For $\ell_1$, use $(-2,0)$ and $(2,2)$: rise $2$, run $4$.

$m_1=\frac{2}{4}=\frac{1}{2}$

For $\ell_2$, use $(-1,1)$ and $(0,-1)$: rise $-2$, run $1$.

$m_2=\frac{-2}{1}=-2$

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{lineblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{linered}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=7mm,color=gridgrey,thin] (-4,-4) grid (4,4);
\draw[black,-{Stealth}] (-4.3,0) -- (4.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,-{Stealth}] (0,-4.3) -- (0,4.4) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \v in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} {
\draw[black] (\v,0.07) -- (\v,-0.07);
\path (\v,-0.12) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};
\draw[black] (0.07,\v) -- (-0.07,\v);
\path (-0.12,\v) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};
}
\path (-0.12,-0.12) node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$0$};
\draw[lineblue,thick] (-4,-1) -- (4,3);
\draw[linered,thick,dashed] (-2.5,4) -- (1.5,-4);
\path (3.3,2.9) node[above,text=lineblue] {$\ell_1$};
\path (1.25,-3.5) node[right,text=linered] {$\ell_2$};
\draw[black,densely dotted,thick] (-2,0) -- (2,0) -- (2,2);
\draw[black,densely dotted,thick] (-1,1) -- (0,1) -- (0,-1);
\foreach \p in {(-2,0),(2,2),(-1,1),(0,-1)} {\fill[black] \p circle (1.5pt);}
\path (1,-0.8) node {$4$};
\path (2.1,1) node[right] {$2$};
\path (-0.5,1.1) node[above] {$1$};
\path (0.25,0.55) node[right] {$-2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$m_1\times m_2=\frac{1}{2}\times(-2)=-1$

The lines are perpendicular.
